<h2 id="frequently-asked-questions">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3 id="what-are-the-requirements-for-an-eb-2-niw">What are the requirements for an EB-2 NIW?</h3>
<p>Two layers. First, qualify for EB-2 through an advanced degree or exceptional ability. Then satisfy the three <em>Dhanasar</em> prongs: an endeavor of substantial merit and national importance, a record showing you can advance it, and a national interest strong enough to justify waiving labor certification.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-self-petition-for-a-green-card-without-an-employer">Can I self-petition for a green card without an employer?</h3>
<p>Yes. USCIS accepts an I-140 filed by the foreign national when a national interest waiver is requested. No employer, no job offer, no labor certification. You still need an approvable EB-2 record and, if you are in the United States, a lawful path to adjustment.</p>
<h3 id="how-long-does-an-eb-2-niw-take">How long does an EB-2 NIW take?</h3>
<p>No single number exists, because two clocks run separately. The I-140 is decided first and can be premium processed. The green card then waits for a visa number, which depends on your category and country of birth and moves monthly with the Visa Bulletin.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-file-an-niw-while-i-am-on-h-1b">Can I file an NIW while I am on H-1B?</h3>
<p>Yes, and many people do. An approved I-140 can also support H-1B extensions beyond the six-year limit in some situations, provided no visa number is available to you yet. Filing the petition is not itself a status problem. Travel while a case is pending needs planning, so ask before you book.</p>
<h3 id="what-happens-if-my-niw-is-denied">What happens if my NIW is denied?</h3>
<p>You have 30 days from the date on the denial notice to act, or 33 days if USCIS mailed it. A motion to reopen or reconsider goes back to the office that decided the case. An appeal goes to the Administrative Appeals Office. If the window closes, a new petition with stronger evidence on the failed prong is often the practical route.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-change-jobs-while-my-niw-is-pending">Can I change jobs while my NIW is pending?</h3>
<p>Usually yes, because the petition rests on your endeavor rather than an employer's job offer. The new role has to stay consistent with the endeavor you described. Move into unrelated work and the petition starts to contradict itself.</p>
